## ServiceLoader.load call sites

Every `ServiceLoader.load(...)`/`loadInstalled(...)` call site found in the app or its
dependencies (SERVICE_LOADING S1), with its service-interface argument resolved by
DATA_FLOW D0-D2's local-value analysis where possible. This step itself is not a
call-graph edge — see "ServiceLoader provider constructor candidates" below for the
provider inventory and model-derived reachable edges.
"Loader" distinguishes the thread context class loader
(`classpath`) from a caller-named `ClassLoader`/`ModuleLayer`
(`explicit`/`module-layer`) or the extension class loader (`installed`) — different
loaders are not guaranteed to see the same providers as a `META-INF/services`
registration above. A caller-named loader recognized from the calling method's own
bytecode — `Thread#getContextClassLoader()` (what `load(Class)` itself uses),
`ClassLoader.getSystemClassLoader()` or `null`, or some class's `getClassLoader()` — is
shown in parentheses and treated as the modeled class path, assuming one application
class loader over every input jar (not true inside servlet containers or nested-jar
launchers); any other loader keeps the visibility gap.
