## ServiceLoader provider constructor candidates

For every interface actually resolved above, this table lists registered providers
with a public no-argument constructor (SERVICE_LOADING S0-S2). The B3 coordinator adds
a model-derived edge only when a reachable `Iterator.next()` or
`ServiceLoader.Provider.get()` call has bounded same-method receiver provenance to the
exact `ServiceLoader.load()` site. `load()` itself is lazy and does not add a
constructor edge. This table is the provider inventory, not proof that every row
produced an edge. A registration whose interface no resolved call site requests is
left out. "Gap" explains why a found provider has no constructor target (for example,
no public no-argument constructor). Receiver flows through fields, static-field
summaries, final instance fields written through `this` in a constructor, and an
exact direct helper returning one of its parameters (substituted from that call
site's argument) are followed using DATA_FLOW D3. A service `Class` or `ClassLoader`
argument that is a parameter of the method calling `load` is resolved from that
method's analyzed callers (D3; up to 3 caller levels and 16 call sites, statically
